Subject: [PATCH] HACK: usb: pci-quirks: skip the xHCI ready wait on the uPD720201

ROCKNIX dropped the wait for every PCI xHCI controller to fix a boot hang
on its SM8550 device with a Renesas uPD720201 (the AYANEO Pocket). Skip
it for that controller only (1912:0014), so other PCI xHCI controllers
keep the wait for the controller to be ready.
---
--- a/drivers/usb/host/pci-quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/pci-quirks.c
@@ -1228,9 +1228,14 @@ static void quirk_usb_handoff_xhci(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 
 	/* Wait for the host controller to be ready before writing any
 	 * operational or runtime registers.  Wait 5 seconds and no more.
+	 * Not on the uPD720201 (the AYANEO Pocket's), whose boot this wait
+	 * hung.
 	 */
-	timeout = handshake(op_reg_base + XHCI_STS_OFFSET, XHCI_STS_CNR, 0,
-			5000000, 10);
+	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_RENESAS && pdev->device == 0x0014)
+		timeout = 0;
+	else
+		timeout = handshake(op_reg_base + XHCI_STS_OFFSET, XHCI_STS_CNR,
+				    0, 5000000, 10);
 	/* Assume a buggy HC and start HC initialization anyway */
 	if (timeout) {
 		val = readl(op_reg_base + XHCI_STS_OFFSET);
